crtsys provides CMake helpers for Windows kernel-mode drivers:

  find_package(crtsys CONFIG REQUIRED)
  crtsys_add_driver(my_driver src/main.cpp)

Optional user-mode content codecs are available with crtsys[content-codecs].
Pinned MsQuic headers are available with crtsys[msquic-headers].

Visual Studio/MSBuild property-page integration is installed with the port.
Run crtsys-vs-init.cmd once from a vcpkg manifest project, then reload the
solution. See share/crtsys/readme.md for driver and entry-point examples.
